<title>BELGIUM: Belgian cartoonist Andre Franquin dies -media.</title>
<headline>Belgian cartoonist Andre Franquin dies -media.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian comic-strip artist Andre Franquin, best known for his cartoon character Gaston Lagaffe which he created for the magazine Spirou, has died at the age of 73, Belgian radio and television said on Sunday.</p>
<p>Franquin, whose work spanned 50 years, had been spending the New Year with relatives in the South of France when he died, they reported.</p>
